========================================
CSS TRANSITION – SYNTAX
========================================

Longhand Syntax
----------------
transition-property: ;
transition-duration: ;
transition-timing-function: ;
transition-delay: ;


Shorthand Syntax:
-----------------
transition: property duration timing-function delay;


Explanation:
------------

1. transition-property
   → Specifies which CSS property should animate.

2. transition-duration
   → Specifies how long the transition takes.
   → (Required for transition to work)

3. transition-timing-function
   → Specifies the speed curve of the transition.
   → Example values: ease, linear, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out

4. transition-delay
   → Specifies how long to wait before starting the transition.


Order of Values:
----------------

1. property          → Which CSS property to animate
2. duration          → How long the animation takes
3. timing-function   → Speed pattern of animation
4. delay             → When the animation should start


Example Structure:
------------------

transition: background-color 0.5s ease 0s;


Important Notes:
----------------

• Duration is mandatory.
• If duration is not given, transition will not work.
• Delay is optional.
• Timing-function is optional.
• Property can be specific (like width, color) or 'all'.